Find the exact volume formed when the region bounded by $x=y-5$, $y=2$ and the $y$-axis is rotated about the $y$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (-4,0)--(1,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.3)--(0,5.8);
\draw[thick] (-3,2)--(0,5);
\draw (-3,2)--(0,2);
\path (1,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,5.8) node[above] {$y$} (-2,4) node[left] {$x=y-5$} (0,2) node[right] {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The region between the right-hand branch of $y=x^{2}-3$ and the $y$-axis extends from $y=-3$ to the height of the point where $x=3$. Find the exact volume formed when this region is rotated about the $y$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(4,0);
\draw[->] (0,-4)--(0,7.5);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=0:3,samples=60] (\x,{(\x)*(\x)-3});
\draw (0,6)--(3,6);
\fill[black] (3,6) circle[radius=1pt];
\path (4,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,7.5) node[above] {$y$} (0,-3) node[left] {$-3$} (3,6) node[right] {$x=3$} (1.7,-2) node[right] {$y=x^{2}-3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the exact volume formed when the region between $y=x^{3}$ and the $y$-axis, from $y=0$ to $y=27$, is rotated about the $y$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=11mm,y=1.5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (-0.4,0)--(4,0);
\draw[->] (0,-2)--(0,32);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=0:3,samples=70] (\x,{(\x)*(\x)*(\x)});
\draw (0,27)--(3,27);
\path (4,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,32) node[above] {$y$} (0,27) node[left] {$27$} (2.5,12) node[right] {$y=x^{3}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the exact volume formed when the region between $y=\sqrt{x-2}$ and the $y$-axis, from $y=0$ to $y=1$, is rotated about the $y$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=25mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (-0.3,0)--(4,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.2)--(0,1.6);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=2:3,samples=60] (\x,{sqrt(\x-2)});
\draw (0,1)--(3,1);
\path (4,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,1.6) node[above] {$y$} (0,1) node[left] {$1$} (2,0) node[below] {$2$} (3,0.55) node[right] {$y=\sqrt{x-2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the exact volume formed when the region between $y=\ln x$ and the $y$-axis, from $y=0$ to $y=2$, is rotated about the $y$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=17mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.7,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.2)--(0,2.8);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=1:7.389056,samples=70] (\x,{ln(\x)});
\draw (0,2)--(7.389056,2);
\path (8.7,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,2.8) node[above] {$y$} (0,2) node[left] {$2$} (1,0) node[below] {$1$} (4,0.9) node[right] {$y=\ln x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the exact volume formed when the region between the positive branch of $y=1/x^{2}$ and the $y$-axis, from $y=2$ to $y=8$, is rotated about the $y$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=35mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (-0.1,0)--(1.3,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.5)--(0,9.5);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=2:8,samples=60,variable=\y] ({1/sqrt(\y)},\y);
\draw (0,2)--({1/sqrt(2)},2);
\draw (0,8)--({1/sqrt(8)},8);
\path (1.3,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,9.5) node[above] {$y$} (0,2) node[left] {$2$} (0,8) node[left] {$8$} (0.6,5) node[right] {$y=1/x^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the exact volume formed when the region bounded by $x=y(y-4)$ and the $y$-axis is rotated about the $y$-axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[->] (-5,0)--(1,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4)--(0,4.8);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=0:4,samples=70,variable=\y] ({\y*(\y-4)},\y);
\path (1,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,4.8) node[above] {$y$} (-4,2) node[left] {$x=y(y-4)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
